-- Arena challenges batch 12/14: rows 276-300 (track: Electrical Machines, category: EEE)

N₁/N₂ = V₁/V₂','{"choices": ["1150 V", "23 V", "46 V", "115 V"], "correct": 2}'::jsonb,'V₂ = V₁ × (N₂/N₁) = 230 × (100/500) = 230 × 0.2 = 46 V. This is a step-down transformer (ratio 5:1). Power is conserved (for ideal transformer): V₁I₁ = V₂I₂.','{multiple_choice}'::text[],0.9) ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

s = (N_s − N_r) / N_s','{"choices": ["6%", "4%", "1%", "10%"], "correct": 1}'::jsonb,'s = (1500 − 1440)/1500 = 60/1500 = 0.04 = 4%. At full load, typical induction motor slip is 2–8%. At no load, slip ≈ 0.1–0.5%. The motor cannot run at exactly synchronous speed (s=0) — no relative motion → no induced rotor EMF → no torque.','{multiple_choice}'::text[],0.88) ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

VR% = (V_NL − V_FL) / V_FL × 100','{"choices": ["10%", "9.09%", "11%", "1%"], "correct": 0}'::jsonb,'VR = (1100 − 1000)/1000 × 100 = 100/1000 × 100 = 10%. Lower VR% is better — means terminal voltage varies less with load. Ideal VR = 0%. Synchronous generators with lagging PF loads have positive VR (voltage drops on load).','{multiple_choice}'::text[],0.8) ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

Step angle = 360° / steps per revolution','{"choices": ["1.8°", "0.9°", "7.5°", "3.6°"], "correct": 0}'::jsonb,'Step angle = 360°/200 = 1.8°. A 1.8° stepper is the most common (NEMA 17, 23 frames). Resolution can be improved by microstepping (1/2, 1/4, ..., 1/256 step) using sinusoidal current shaping — up to 200 × 256 = 51,200 microsteps/rev.','{multiple_choice}'::text[],0.87) ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

η = Output/(Output + Losses)','{"choices": ["98.5%", "99%", "97%", "98%"], "correct": 0}'::jsonb,'Output = 100,000 W (100 kVA × UPF). Total losses = 500 + 1000 = 1500 W. η = 100,000/(100,000+1500) × 100 = 100,000/101,500 = 98.52% ≈ 98.5%.','{multiple_choice}'::text[],0.75) ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;
